{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XuV2JfBpiJqjz9V8yHq4mF","type":"tool_result","content":"## 14. Flow field\n\n- `new E.FlowField(map, o = {}) → flow`: new E.FlowField(map, { step: 2, climb: 0, drop: 0, jump: 0 }): distances over the tops a body can stand on (E.HEIGHTS). With no options it covers the floor (and walls no higher than step, which bodies walk over); a target on a roof gets a field across the roofs it connects to\n- `new E.FlowField({ step, climb, drop })`: next-door cells connect when their tops differ by at most step, or going up by up to climb and down by up to drop (agents that climb walls or hop down)\n- `new E.FlowField({ jump })`: (world units) links tops across a gap that a jump clears, straight along a row or column, by map.landing's rules (up to jumpRise higher, 11, and jumpDrop lower, 18): an agent with E.Mover's leap chases across roofs. With jump, distances are travel: a jump of k cells costs k, and a climb 1 plus its rise in cells (climbing is slow), so a chase leaps a gap rather than drop into the street and climb back up\n- `flow.dir(x, y, fx, fy)`: normalized ground direction to walk from (x, y) toward the target (straight at it where the field doesn't reach)\n- `flow.next(x, y)` †: the next cell to head for from (x, y): { x, y, z (its center and top), kind: 'walk' | 'climb' | 'drop' | 'jump', edge (how far (x, y) is from the side of its cell it leaves by) }, or null where the field doesn't reach (or at the target). An AI standing on the ground presses jump for a 'climb' or a 'jump' once edge is under its radius plus a little (E.Mover climbs or leaps; a press in the air would be kept for the landing)\n- `flow.update(x, y)`: aim the field at a world point; it rebuilds only when the target's cell or the map (map.version) changes\n- `flow.climb`: how much higher a next-door top may be (an agent that climbs walls)\n- `flow.d`: each cell's distance in steps to the target cell (1e9 where it can't get there), row by row\n- `flow.drop`: how much lower (an agent that hops down)\n- `flow.jump` †: the widest gap jumped (world units, 0 = none)\n- `flow.jumpDrop`, `flow.jumpRise` †: how much higher and lower a jump may land\n- `flow.map`: the map it paths over\n- `flow.step`: the height difference walked over freely (2)\n- `flow.tx = -1`, `flow.ty = -1`: the target's cell\n----\n1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1063:- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the music clock, scheduled with the music: a rhythm game's calls and claps) }\n1075:- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n1134:- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)\n1543:- `new E.Rhythm(game, o = {}) → rhythm` †: new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual\n1570:- `rhythm.voice` †: the calls' sound\n----\n459:- `new E.Game({ menu })`: the pause, settings and controls screens ({ items, settings, controls, quit } adjusts them, false leaves them out)\n----\n1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n----\n// A headless test of the template game: the engine and game.js run in Node with no screen (new E.Game is headless where\n// there is no DOM), driven by fixed steps (game.advance) and scripted input (input.tap, input.hold), and read through\n// game.debug.snapshot(). Run it: node game/test.mjs (exit code 1 on a failure). Write one like it for your game.\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n\nconst ctx = { console };\nvm.createContext(ctx);\nfor (const f of ['../my-3d2dge.js', './game.js']) vm.runInContext(readFileSync(new URL(f, import.meta.url), 'utf8'), ctx, { filename: f });\nconst E = ctx.My3D2dge, game = E.current, I = game.input, snap = () => game.debug.snapshot();\nlet failed = 0;\nconst check = (what, ok, detail = '') => { console.log((ok ? 'ok   ' : 'FAIL ') + what + (ok ? '' : ': ' + detail)); if (!ok) failed++; };\n\ngame.advance(.5);\ncheck('the title waits for start', snap().scene === 'title', JSON.stringify(snap()));\nI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\ncheck('start begins play', snap().scene === 'play', JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// climb: stand facing the roof's west wall (cells 7-9 of rows 4-6: x 112-160, y 64-112), press jump to take hold, then\n// climb with up (up the screen is up the wall) until it pulls up onto the top\ngame.debug.teleport(100, 88, 0, 0);\nI.tap('jump'); game.advance(.1);\ncheck('jump next to a wall takes hold of it', snap().climbing, JSON.stringify(snap()));\nI.hold('up'); game.advance(.6); I.hold('up', false); game.advance(1);\ncheck('climbing up pulls up onto the roof', !snap().climbing && snap().hero[2] === 32, JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// take the gem (on the roof's middle cell), then hop down into the street with it\ngame.debug.teleport(136, 88, 32, 0); game.advance(.1);\ncheck('walking onto the gem takes it', snap().got, JSON.stringify(snap()));\ngame.debug.teleport(156, 120, 32, Math.PI / 2); I.hold('down'); game.advance(1.5); I.hold('down', false); game.advance(.5);\ncheck('back in the street with the gem wins', snap().scene === 'end' && snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// get seen: stand in front of the guard, in the open, until its alert fills\nI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\nconst [gx, gy, gf] = snap().guard;\ngame.debug.teleport(gx + Math.cos(gf) * 40, gy + Math.sin(gf) * 40, 0, gf + Math.PI);\ngame.advance(2.5);\ncheck('the guard catches a hero it sees', snap().scene === 'end' && !snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\ncheck('no errors', !game.errors.length, game.errors.map(e => e.message).join(' | '));\n\nconsole.log(failed ? `${failed} check(s) failed` : 'all checks passed');\nprocess.exit(failed ? 1 : 0);","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4accd60f-1720-4154-a575-c0b8f1413e9f","uuid":"833c240e-9029-429c-a873-271ae667757b","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:00:57.265Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## 14. Flow field\n\n- `new E.FlowField(map, o = {}) → flow`: new E.FlowField(map, { step: 2, climb: 0, drop: 0, jump: 0 }): distances over the tops a body can stand on (E.HEIGHTS). With no options it covers the floor (and walls no higher than step, which bodies walk over); a target on a roof gets a field across the roofs it connects to\n- `new E.FlowField({ step, climb, drop })`: next-door cells connect when their tops differ by at most step, or going up by up to climb and down by up to drop (agents that climb walls or hop down)\n- `new E.FlowField({ jump })`: (world units) links tops across a gap that a jump clears, straight along a row or column, by map.landing's rules (up to jumpRise higher, 11, and jumpDrop lower, 18): an agent with E.Mover's leap chases across roofs. With jump, distances are travel: a jump of k cells costs k, and a climb 1 plus its rise in cells (climbing is slow), so a chase leaps a gap rather than drop into the street and climb back up\n- `flow.dir(x, y, fx, fy)`: normalized ground direction to walk from (x, y) toward the target (straight at it where the field doesn't reach)\n- `flow.next(x, y)` †: the next cell to head for from (x, y): { x, y, z (its center and top), kind: 'walk' | 'climb' | 'drop' | 'jump', edge (how far (x, y) is from the side of its cell it leaves by) }, or null where the field doesn't reach (or at the target). An AI standing on the ground presses jump for a 'climb' or a 'jump' once edge is under its radius plus a little (E.Mover climbs or leaps; a press in the air would be kept for the landing)\n- `flow.update(x, y)`: aim the field at a world point; it rebuilds only when the target's cell or the map (map.version) changes\n- `flow.climb`: how much higher a next-door top may be (an agent that climbs walls)\n- `flow.d`: each cell's distance in steps to the target cell (1e9 where it can't get there), row by row\n- `flow.drop`: how much lower (an agent that hops down)\n- `flow.jump` †: the widest gap jumped (world units, 0 = none)\n- `flow.jumpDrop`, `flow.jumpRise` †: how much higher and lower a jump may land\n- `flow.map`: the map it paths over\n- `flow.step`: the height difference walked over freely (2)\n- `flow.tx = -1`, `flow.ty = -1`: the target's cell\n----\n1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1063:- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the music clock, scheduled with the music: a rhythm game's calls and claps) }\n1075:- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n1134:- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)\n1543:- `new E.Rhythm(game, o = {}) → rhythm` †: new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual\n1570:- `rhythm.voice` †: the calls' sound\n----\n459:- `new E.Game({ menu })`: the pause, settings and controls screens ({ items, settings, controls, quit } adjusts them, false leaves them out)\n----\n1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n----\n// A headless test of the template game: the engine and game.js run in Node with no screen (new E.Game is headless where\n// there is no DOM), driven by fixed steps (game.advance) and scripted input (input.tap, input.hold), and read through\n// game.debug.snapshot(). Run it: node game/test.mjs (exit code 1 on a failure). Write one like it for your game.\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n\nconst ctx = { console };\nvm.createContext(ctx);\nfor (const f of ['../my-3d2dge.js', './game.js']) vm.runInContext(readFileSync(new URL(f, import.meta.url), 'utf8'), ctx, { filename: f });\nconst E = ctx.My3D2dge, game = E.current, I = game.input, snap = () => game.debug.snapshot();\nlet failed = 0;\nconst check = (what, ok, detail = '') => { console.log((ok ? 'ok   ' : 'FAIL ') + what + (ok ? '' : ': ' + detail)); if (!ok) failed++; };\n\ngame.advance(.5);\ncheck('the title waits for start', snap().scene === 'title', JSON.stringify(snap()));\nI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\ncheck('start begins play', snap().scene === 'play', JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// climb: stand facing the roof's west wall (cells 7-9 of rows 4-6: x 112-160, y 64-112), press jump to take hold, then\n// climb with up (up the screen is up the wall) until it pulls up onto the top\ngame.debug.teleport(100, 88, 0, 0);\nI.tap('jump'); game.advance(.1);\ncheck('jump next to a wall takes hold of it', snap().climbing, JSON.stringify(snap()));\nI.hold('up'); game.advance(.6); I.hold('up', false); game.advance(1);\ncheck('climbing up pulls up onto the roof', !snap().climbing && snap().hero[2] === 32, JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// take the gem (on the roof's middle cell), then hop down into the street with it\ngame.debug.teleport(136, 88, 32, 0); game.advance(.1);\ncheck('walking onto the gem takes it', snap().got, JSON.stringify(snap()));\ngame.debug.teleport(156, 120, 32, Math.PI / 2); I.hold('down'); game.advance(1.5); I.hold('down', false); game.advance(.5);\ncheck('back in the street with the gem wins', snap().scene === 'end' && snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// get seen: stand in front of the guard, in the open, until its alert fills\nI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\nconst [gx, gy, gf] = snap().guard;\ngame.debug.teleport(gx + Math.cos(gf) * 40, gy + Math.sin(gf) * 40, 0, gf + Math.PI);\ngame.advance(2.5);\ncheck('the guard catches a hero it sees', snap().scene === 'end' && !snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\ncheck('no errors', !game.errors.length, game.errors.map(e => e.message).join(' | '));\n\nconsole.log(failed ? `${failed} check(s) failed` : 'all checks passed');\nprocess.exit(failed ? 1 : 0);","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XuV2JfBpiJqjz9V8yHq4mF","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
